{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_936d0cb7de5843a0a384597e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-18 15:43:21 GMT\n2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-18 22:43:21 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n3\tCoding-Agent: codex\n4\tSession-ID: 01a1ea51-a87d-7062-ae12-e6c1c169b48c\n5\t\n6\t# cc4 r2 bounded run declaration v1 (before budget measurements)\n7\t\n8\tRevision: post `2687ab0cf03ebaa232be49a2333347d12a71d9a3` plus the cc4 test-only patch;\n9\tpre-port `8afd82f5e99d0f2b2d38a5f53b292105fdead688` (first parent of\n10\tport merge `309fe842`). Input corpus: the eight entries in `replay-artifacts`\n11\tin `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`: destructuring/float/metadata/duplicate\n12\tnative and argument-vector programs, lower-unit with bundled library, prelude,\n13\tmacro twin with its producing log, second-token admission, and freshly published\n14\t`yang.call` and `clj` with their complete side artifacts. No runtime tracing.\n15\t\n16\tThe cc3 v2.1 baselines are reference observations, NOT cc4 measurements:\n17\trows 312886 B, relation 856315 B, retained compiled-inclusive maximum\n18\t8924640 B, peak 272026880 B, pipeline maximum 772 ms. Its per-fixture ceilings\n19\twere 2 MB/artifact, 4 MB/aggregate, 12 MB retained, 1 GiB peak, 10 s pipeline.\n20\tThe following finite ceilings scale these to an eight-member closure and allow\n21\thost representation differences. A sample exceeding a bound FAILS this run;\n22\tno bound will be raised in place.\n23\t\n24\t| Quantity | Finite ceiling, both revisions, every host/configuration |\n25\t|---|---:|\n26\t| Unique canonical rows / occurrence positions / application positions, corpus | 50000 / 100000 / 10000 |\n27\t| Maximum path depth / encoded application paths, corpus | 256 / 8000000 B |\n28\t| Static side bytes per artifact / aggregate closure | 2000000 B / 32000000 B |\n29\t| Aggregate retained compiled-inclusive holder | 96000000 B incremental used heap |\n30\t| Absolute sampled heap peak | 2147483648 B |\n31\t| Absolute process-tree RSS peak, where heap unavailable | 4294967296 B |\n32\t| Retained process RSS, where heap unavailable | 4294967296 B (absolute; not heap-comparable) |\n33\t| Warm pipeline / cold pipeline (excludes toolchain compilation) | 80000 / 160000 ms |\n34\t| Each compile/expand/project/publish/load/query stage | 80000 ms |\n35\t| S−B allowed pipeline / retained / aggregate static bytes | 40000 ms / 96000000 B / 32000000 B |\n36\t| Trace records / capacity / trace bytes | 0 / 0 / 0 (trace disabled throughout) |\n37\t\n38\tStorage aggregate uses 8 × cc3's 4 MB ceiling; retained uses 8 × 12 MB.\n39\tPeak heap uses 2 × cc3's 1 GiB ceiling; process RSS includes runtime/native\n40\tallocator/executable pages and therefore has a separately named 4 GiB ceiling.\n41\tWarm time uses 8 × 10 s; cold time is twice warm. Depth and input limits are\n42\tconservative finite preflight rejection bounds for this small pinned corpus,\n43\tincluding generated/prelude closure. No tagged execution is part of cc4.\n44\t\n45\tB uses the same compiling inputs with C1 metadata removed before projection,\n46\tlowering/publication/persistence/load/query; S retains annotations and enables\n47\tthose side operations. Both disable runtime trace. The production compiler\n48\tcurrently always annotates: the compile cost common to B/S includes that work.\n49\tS−B therefore measures downstream static-artifact overhead and cannot establish\n50\tthe annotation producer's incremental compile cost. This limitation must appear\n51\twith the result; no claim of total zero compile overhead is permitted.\n52\t\n53\tProcedure: one cold build, one discarded warmup, 3 warm pipeline samples per\n54\tconfiguration; 5 retained samples where forced GC is available (JVM and Node).\n55\tHold one complete corpus at a time, release each holder before the next sample.\n56\tRecord every sample and use MAXIMUM for every verdict. JVM: GC-pinned\n57\tRuntime totalMemory−freeMemory, 2 ms sampled used heap. Node: exposed GC,\n58\tprocess.memoryUsage().heapUsed and synchronous stage-boundary heap samples\n59\t(mark as a lower bound on the true transient peak). Dart/Jolt: named process RSS\n60\tif heap counters are unavailable; process RSS is never substituted for a heap\n61\tdelta without recording the changed metric. Warm time excludes toolchain build;\n62\tclass-loading/startup must be identified separately. Measure pre and post using\n63\tthe same harness and inputs; any pre/post shift is allocated to port Phase 2\n64\t`d60038ef` as directed, with unrelated base differences stated as confounders.\n65\tD1 is dissolved and no correspondence acceptance is claimed.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"0ad8fb41-06e0-4a23-9ce1-cd2bc6cc313c","timestamp":"2026-11-19T22:03:58.373Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1795016601236-cc4-r2-budget-declaration-v1.md","content":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-18 15:43:21 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-18 22:43:21 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a1ea51-a87d-7062-ae12-e6c1c169b48c\n\n# cc4 r2 bounded run declaration v1 (before budget measurements)\n\nRevision: post `2687ab0cf03ebaa232be49a2333347d12a71d9a3` plus the cc4 test-only patch;\npre-port `8afd82f5e99d0f2b2d38a5f53b292105fdead688` (first parent of\nport merge `309fe842`). Input corpus: the eight entries in `replay-artifacts`\nin `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`: destructuring/float/metadata/duplicate\nnative and argument-vector programs, lower-unit with bundled library, prelude,\nmacro twin with its producing log, second-token admission, and freshly published\n`yang.call` and `clj` with their complete side artifacts. No runtime tracing.\n\nThe cc3 v2.1 baselines are reference observations, NOT cc4 measurements:\nrows 312886 B, relation 856315 B, retained compiled-inclusive maximum\n8924640 B, peak 272026880 B, pipeline maximum 772 ms. Its per-fixture ceilings\nwere 2 MB/artifact, 4 MB/aggregate, 12 MB retained, 1 GiB peak, 10 s pipeline.\nThe following finite ceilings scale these to an eight-member closure and allow\nhost representation differences. A sample exceeding a bound FAILS this run;\nno bound will be raised in place.\n\n| Quantity | Finite ceiling, both revisions, every host/configuration |\n|---|---:|\n| Unique canonical rows / occurrence positions / application positions, corpus | 50000 / 100000 / 10000 |\n| Maximum path depth / encoded application paths, corpus | 256 / 8000000 B |\n| Static side bytes per artifact / aggregate closure | 2000000 B / 32000000 B |\n| Aggregate retained compiled-inclusive holder | 96000000 B incremental used heap |\n| Absolute sampled heap peak | 2147483648 B |\n| Absolute process-tree RSS peak, where heap unavailable | 4294967296 B |\n| Retained process RSS, where heap unavailable | 4294967296 B (absolute; not heap-comparable) |\n| Warm pipeline / cold pipeline (excludes toolchain compilation) | 80000 / 160000 ms |\n| Each compile/expand/project/publish/load/query stage | 80000 ms |\n| S−B allowed pipeline / retained / aggregate static bytes | 40000 ms / 96000000 B / 32000000 B |\n| Trace records / capacity / trace bytes | 0 / 0 / 0 (trace disabled throughout) |\n\nStorage aggregate uses 8 × cc3's 4 MB ceiling; retained uses 8 × 12 MB.\nPeak heap uses 2 × cc3's 1 GiB ceiling; process RSS includes runtime/native\nallocator/executable pages and therefore has a separately named 4 GiB ceiling.\nWarm time uses 8 × 10 s; cold time is twice warm. Depth and input limits are\nconservative finite preflight rejection bounds for this small pinned corpus,\nincluding generated/prelude closure. No tagged execution is part of cc4.\n\nB uses the same compiling inputs with C1 metadata removed before projection,\nlowering/publication/persistence/load/query; S retains annotations and enables\nthose side operations. Both disable runtime trace. The production compiler\ncurrently always annotates: the compile cost common to B/S includes that work.\nS−B therefore measures downstream static-artifact overhead and cannot establish\nthe annotation producer's incremental compile cost. This limitation must appear\nwith the result; no claim of total zero compile overhead is permitted.\n\nProcedure: one cold build, one discarded warmup, 3 warm pipeline samples per\nconfiguration; 5 retained samples where forced GC is available (JVM and Node).\nHold one complete corpus at a time, release each holder before the next sample.\nRecord every sample and use MAXIMUM for every verdict. JVM: GC-pinned\nRuntime totalMemory−freeMemory, 2 ms sampled used heap. Node: exposed GC,\nprocess.memoryUsage().heapUsed and synchronous stage-boundary heap samples\n(mark as a lower bound on the true transient peak). Dart/Jolt: named process RSS\nif heap counters are unavailable; process RSS is never substituted for a heap\ndelta without recording the changed metric. Warm time excludes toolchain build;\nclass-loading/startup must be identified separately. Measure pre and post using\nthe same harness and inputs; any pre/post shift is allocated to port Phase 2\n`d60038ef` as directed, with unrelated base differences stated as confounders.\nD1 is dissolved and no correspondence acceptance is claimed.\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_936d0cb7de5843a0a384597e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
