{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261120062049039d727d91b34820","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The pre-port tree's `mise.toml` (from the archive) is untrusted when mise runs with cwd inside target/. The outer runs work because the worktree's mise.toml is already trusted. Fix: run the child with MISE_CONFIG_FILE env pointing to the outer one, or `mise trust` that path, or simplest: set `MISE_TRUSTED_CONFIGS_PATHS`... Cleanest: copy the TRUSTED mise state — mise trust writes to ~/.local/share/mise/trusted-configs (a text list). I can append the path via the child env `MISE_YES=1`? The least invasive: run the child with cwd=worktree root but pass the pre-port dir via absolute paths for -cp and... clojure -Spath needs cwd IN the tree (paths are relative to its deps.edn). Alternative: `cd target/cc4-preport && MISE_CONFIG_FILE=../../mise.toml clojure ...`? MISE_CONFIG_FILE redirects the config. Hmm — or trust it: `mise trust ~/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/target/cc4-preport/mise.toml`? The trust command takes paths. Try that first in the child.","signature":"db32a8a5ae62404993308bb0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"2b268d07-00e9-4ab6-809f-4edb208e5638","timestamp":"2026-11-19T22:21:00.527Z","thinking_duration_ms":4470,"thinking_display":"updates"}
