{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026112006250682e1e2ceb07c4ebf","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The corpus builder. My common-corpus file: a copy with an `excluded` set parameter, skipping the excluded members (the lower-unit LINE never evaluated when excluded — wrap each entry in a conditional). To stay faithful I'll copy the fn body verbatim and only wrap the result vector entries + the lower-unit COMPUTATION (which is inline in the vector — `(projected :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit forms) ...)` — evaluated when building the vector! So gate the whole entry: `(if (excluded :lower-unit) nothing (projected ...))` — build the vector then `(remove excluded)`. The lower-unit EVALUATION inside the vector literal happens before remove — must guard: make the vector entries lazy? Simplest: `(cond-> [] (not (excluded :lower-unit)) (conj (projected :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit forms) ...)) ...)`. Copy the fn with that one conditional.\n\nThe corpus file requires: walk, encoder, yang, clj-prelude, call, publish, mem, jing, vm, macro + expand-like-the-repl (PRIVATE in the callsite test!) — the macro member needs it. Copy expand-like-the-repl into the corpus file too (it's a helper: seed-store/make-ctx/expand-batch — self-contained). And publish-registry (private: default-registry + cell + data module with max-items).\n\nSo `yang/cc4_corpus.clj` = private copies of publish-registry + expand-like-the-repl + replay-artifacts-with-exclusions. It duplicates ~70 lines of the cohort definition — the divergence risk is acceptable for one measurement round and the file cites its source (file + SHA of the copied origin) for fidelity. The runner then requires yang.cc4-corpus instead of the callsite test ENTIRELY (drops the test-ns dependency — cleaner for pre-port: no need to carry the whole callsite test into the pre-port tree!).\n\nRewrite: cc4_corpus.clj (new), runner requires it, takes exclusion via second arg (\"EX=lower-unit\" comma list or \"EX=none\"). Corpus file + runner are the two carried files. The pre-port tree needs NO callsite test copy anymore.\n\nAlso the corpus's `:yin/if`/`:yin/literal` macro forms and `^:replay` metadata — same at both pins? The corpus compiles :native/:argument-vector at pre-port ✓ probed. The macro member: `(yin/if ...)` forms — yang/compile-program handles them at pre-port? The cohort came from cc4 (post-port era, base 2687ab0c which is AFTER the port). The :macro member compiles `(yin/if (yin/literal true) x ...)` — compile-program treats `(yin/if ...)` as an APPLICATION (ordinary call) — fine at any pin. The publishes (call/module-spec, clj-prelude/module-spec, publish-module!, published-call-site-table) — signatures at pre-port? UNKNOWN — probe empirically after building.\n\nAlso `replay-artifacts` references `expand-like-the-repl` with tokens — pre-port macro/seed-store/make-ctx/expand-batch exist (the cc2-era API) — probe.\n\nBuild the corpus file now.","signature":"cee822051052461693846af2"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"a3704aea-4f68-4642-8271-cfaf05941fa8","timestamp":"2026-11-19T22:25:21.897Z","thinking_duration_ms":10336,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026112006250682e1e2ceb07c4ebf","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_8dec6c3a284b486a851b976c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsrc = '''(ns yang.cc4-corpus\n  \"The cc4 budget common corpus: a faithful copy of the pinned cohort\n   builder test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc/replay-artifacts at\n   origin/master 2175252d (sha256 of that file at that pin is recorded in\n   the budget findings), factored with one knob: an EXCLUDED id set, so\n   members the PRE-port pin refuses (the lower-unit member: pre-port\n   check-top-level-discard! rejects a may-fail non-final form, which the\n   port-era corpus relies on) can be omitted from BOTH revisions of the\n   measurement, keeping the pre/post corpus identical. Nothing else\n   differs from the cohort definition; the equality gate itself continues\n   to use the cohort in the test namespace.\"\n  (:require [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n(def ^:private publish-registry\n  (-> (module/default-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})))\n\n(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n  [ast]\n  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n                (macro/make-ctx {:token :cc4-budget/standard-forms\n                                 :source-medium :cc4-budget/standard-forms})\n                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"cc4-budget\"\n                             :source-medium :program-in\n                             :store store})]\n    {:ctx ctx\n     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n\n(defn replay-corpus\n  \"The pinned eight-member corpus; `excluded` is a set of member ids to\n   omit (recorded in the findings with the exact reason).\"\n  ([] (replay-corpus #{}))\n  ([excluded]\n   (let [prepare (fn [ast]\n                   (walk/postwalk (fn [n]\n                                    (if (map? n)\n                                      (dissoc n :yang/call-site) n))\n                                  ast))\n         forms (quote [(defn replay\n                         [x]\n                         (let [[a b] [x 1.5]]\n                           (+ (identity ^:replay a)\n                              (identity ^:replay a) b)))\n                       (replay 2)])\n         projected (fn [id ast token]\n                     (let [ast (prepare ast)\n                           p (encoder/project\n                               (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\n                       {:id id :compiled ast\n                        :tree (first (:yin/batch p))\n                        :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)}))\n         ast (yang/compile-program forms)\n         macro-ast (yang/compile-program\n                     (quote [(defmacro twin\n                               [x]\n                               (yin/if (yin/literal true) x\n                                       (yin/application (yin/variable f)\n                                                        [(yin/literal 1)])))\n                             (defn f\n                               [x]\n                               x)\n                             (twin (f 1))]))\n         expansion (:result (expand-like-the-repl (prepare macro-ast)))\n         store (mem/create-content-mem)\n         call-spec (update (call/module-spec publish-registry) :ast prepare)\n         call-result (publish/publish-module! store call-spec)\n         clj-spec (update (clj-prelude/module-spec\n                            publish-registry (:address call-result))\n                          :ast prepare)\n         clj-result (publish/publish-module! store clj-spec)\n         published (fn [id result spec]\n                     (let [table (publish/published-call-site-table store result)]\n                       {:id id :compiled (:ast spec)\n                        :tree (or (:tree table)\n                                  (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:ast spec)))\n                        :rows (or (:rows table) [])\n                        :addresses (assoc (dissoc (:call-sites result) :origin)\n                                          :manifest (:address result))\n                        :published-payloads\n                        (when (:call-sites result)\n                          (mapv #(jing/get store % nil)\n                                (map (:call-sites result)\n                                     [:table :provenance :record])))\n                        :provenance (publish/published-instruction-provenance\n                                      store result)}))\n         members (cond-> []\n                   (not (contains? excluded :native))\n                   (conj (projected :native ast \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :argument-vector))\n                   (conj (projected :argument-vector\n                                    (yang/compile-program forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :lower-unit))\n                   (conj (projected :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit forms)\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :prelude))\n                   (conj (projected :prelude clj-prelude/module-uast\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :macro))\n                   (conj {:id :macro :compiled (prepare macro-ast)\n                          :status (:status expansion)\n                          :tree (macro/packet->row-set (:tree expansion))\n                          :rows (:frontend-metadata expansion)\n                          :expansion-log (:log expansion)})\n                   (not (contains? excluded :negative))\n                   (conj (projected :negative ast \"admission-b\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :yang.call))\n                   (conj (published :yang.call call-result call-spec))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :clj))\n                   (conj (published :clj clj-result clj-spec)))]\n     members)))\n'''\nPath(\"test/yang/cc4_corpus.clj\").write_text(src)\nprint(\"corpus file written\")\nPYEOF","description":"Write the common corpus file"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"856da5bb-0a29-4724-bb09-a2c1c1a68100","timestamp":"2026-11-19T22:25:32.114Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_8dec6c3a284b486a851b976c":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsrc = '''(ns yang.cc4-corpus\n  \"The cc4 budget common corpus: a faithful copy of the pinned cohort\n   builder test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc/replay-artifacts at\n   origin/master 2175252d (sha256 of that file at that pin is recorded in\n   the budget findings), factored with one knob: an EXCLUDED id set, so\n   members the PRE-port pin refuses (the lower-unit member: pre-port\n   check-top-level-discard! rejects a may-fail non-final form, which the\n   port-era corpus relies on) can be omitted from BOTH revisions of the\n   measurement, keeping the pre/post corpus identical. Nothing else\n   differs from the cohort definition; the equality gate itself continues\n   to use the cohort in the test namespace.\"\n  (:require [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n(def ^:private publish-registry\n  (-> (module/default-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})))\n\n(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n  [ast]\n  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n                (macro/make-ctx {:token :cc4-budget/standard-forms\n                                 :source-medium :cc4-budget/standard-forms})\n                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"cc4-budget\"\n                             :source-medium :program-in\n                             :store store})]\n    {:ctx ctx\n     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n\n(defn replay-corpus\n  \"The pinned eight-member corpus; `excluded` is a set of member ids to\n   omit (recorded in the findings with the exact reason).\"\n  ([] (replay-corpus #{}))\n  ([excluded]\n   (let [prepare (fn [ast]\n                   (walk/postwalk (fn [n]\n                                    (if (map? n)\n                                      (dissoc n :yang/call-site) n))\n                                  ast))\n         forms (quote [(defn replay\n                         [x]\n                         (let [[a b] [x 1.5]]\n                           (+ (identity ^:replay a)\n                              (identity ^:replay a) b)))\n                       (replay 2)])\n         projected (fn [id ast token]\n                     (let [ast (prepare ast)\n                           p (encoder/project\n                               (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\n                       {:id id :compiled ast\n                        :tree (first (:yin/batch p))\n                        :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)}))\n         ast (yang/compile-program forms)\n         macro-ast (yang/compile-program\n                     (quote [(defmacro twin\n                               [x]\n                               (yin/if (yin/literal true) x\n                                       (yin/application (yin/variable f)\n                                                        [(yin/literal 1)])))\n                             (defn f\n                               [x]\n                               x)\n                             (twin (f 1))]))\n         expansion (:result (expand-like-the-repl (prepare macro-ast)))\n         store (mem/create-content-mem)\n         call-spec (update (call/module-spec publish-registry) :ast prepare)\n         call-result (publish/publish-module! store call-spec)\n         clj-spec (update (clj-prelude/module-spec\n                            publish-registry (:address call-result))\n                          :ast prepare)\n         clj-result (publish/publish-module! store clj-spec)\n         published (fn [id result spec]\n                     (let [table (publish/published-call-site-table store result)]\n                       {:id id :compiled (:ast spec)\n                        :tree (or (:tree table)\n                                  (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:ast spec)))\n                        :rows (or (:rows table) [])\n                        :addresses (assoc (dissoc (:call-sites result) :origin)\n                                          :manifest (:address result))\n                        :published-payloads\n                        (when (:call-sites result)\n                          (mapv #(jing/get store % nil)\n                                (map (:call-sites result)\n                                     [:table :provenance :record])))\n                        :provenance (publish/published-instruction-provenance\n                                      store result)}))\n         members (cond-> []\n                   (not (contains? excluded :native))\n                   (conj (projected :native ast \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :argument-vector))\n                   (conj (projected :argument-vector\n                                    (yang/compile-program forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :lower-unit))\n                   (conj (projected :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit forms)\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :prelude))\n                   (conj (projected :prelude clj-prelude/module-uast\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :macro))\n                   (conj {:id :macro :compiled (prepare macro-ast)\n                          :status (:status expansion)\n                          :tree (macro/packet->row-set (:tree expansion))\n                          :rows (:frontend-metadata expansion)\n                          :expansion-log (:log expansion)})\n                   (not (contains? excluded :negative))\n                   (conj (projected :negative ast \"admission-b\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :yang.call))\n                   (conj (published :yang.call call-result call-spec))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :clj))\n                   (conj (published :clj clj-result clj-spec)))]\n     members)))\n'''\nPath(\"test/yang/cc4_corpus.clj\").write_text(src)\nprint(\"corpus file written\")\nPYEOF","description":"Write the common corpus file"}}}
