{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261120062532fe8a57d444a043fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — one fidelity issue in my corpus copy: the original macro form uses `(yin/variable 'f)` with a QUOTE inside the quoted form — I wrote `(yin/variable f)` (dropped the inner quote because of my no-quote discipline!). In the original: `(yin/application (yin/variable 'f) [(yin/literal 1)])` INSIDE a `'`-quoted form — the quoted form contains `(quote f)`. My version has bare `f` — a DIFFERENT program (variable f vs quoted 'f)! The original cohort's macro: `(yin/variable 'f)` — under the outer quote it's `(quote f)`. Also `^:replay` metadata ✓ preserved via `^:replay`? I wrote `^:replay a` ✓.\n\nFix: write the macro form with `(quote f)` instead of `'f`:\n`(yin/application (yin/variable (quote f)) [(yin/literal 1)])` — inside my `(quote [...])` outer → the form contains (quote f) ✓ identical to the original's `'f`.\n\nAlso check my `forms` — original has `^:replay a` twice ✓ mine ✓.\n\nUpdate the runner to use the corpus + exclusions arg, fix the macro form, and re-verify the corpus produces the SAME artifacts as the cohort at the post pin (roots equality check — a fidelity assertion I can add to a probe: compare ids + roots between cohort/replay-artifacts and corpus/replay-corpus at post — strong evidence the copy is faithful).","signature":"e72c3755ab3244e3b725fca1"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"dfe50b65-352d-4f38-8b77-0e52fb0dfaa6","timestamp":"2026-11-19T22:25:43.782Z","thinking_duration_ms":5229,"thinking_display":"updates"}
