{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611200638139c14ee74cb3141ac","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"REVEALING: per-member COUNTS are IDENTICAL (rows 35/494/499/225/15... same trees) but the payload SIZES differ wildly:\n- darkstar member1 (native): sizes [4149, 8328, 425] (rows=4149, relation=8328, record=425)\n- jupiter member1: sizes [977, 4, 425] (rows=977, relation=4!!, record=425)\n\nThe `relation` payload is 4 BYTES on jupiter vs 8,328 on darkstar — 4 bytes = `[]` EMPTY VECTOR! And rows differ 4149 vs 977. Same counts, same image digest... \n\nThe rows payload: `(jing/materialize! store rows)` where rows = the member's :rows (frontend metadata). 4149 vs 977 for the SAME tree+metadata?? The rows include the C1 marker rows AND position/metadata rows — identical inputs → identical bytes → identical sizes. UNLESS THE RUNNER DIFFERS: darkstar post8 ran runner v2 which read `rows` from... WAIT — v2's pipeline had `rows` bound from `(cohort/replay-artifacts)` artifacts ✓ same.\n\nOH!!! I BET I KNOW: **the corpus's `prepare` for S**! My corpus defines `prepare` as a LOCAL fn `(fn [ast] (walk/postwalk (dissoc :yang/call-site)))` applied ONLY where explicitly called (projected calls prepare ast). For the S config (annotated?=true), the COHORT's prepare = identity. My corpus: `(fn [ast] (walk/postwalk ...))` — THE CORPUS ALWAYS STRIPS for `projected`!! Look at my corpus code:\n\n```clojure\nprepare (fn [ast] (walk/postwalk ...))   ;; ALWAYS strips!\n...\nprojected (fn [id ast token]\n            (let [ast (prepare ast) ...\n```\n\nThe cohort: `prepare (if annotated? identity #(strip))` — for S (annotated), prepare = identity! My corpus IGNORES annotated? and ALWAYS strips the :yang/call-site keys — SO MY CORPUS RUNS B AS B AND \"S\" AS B TOO?! But then the image digests would match B... they DO differ between my post7-B and... wait no: post7-B digest 3ef61619 = post7-S digest 3ef61619 — images equal (expected either way — :yang/call-site doesn't affect rows). The S-specific rows (the C1 marker metadata rows!) — stripping :yang/call-site BEFORE encoder/project removes the marker → the projected :rows LOSE the marker rows → S's rows payload smaller (977 vs 4149) and the relation (call-provenance — derived from rows!) EMPTY (4 bytes) on jupiter!!\n\nSo jupiter's \"S\" runs were actually running **B-shaped corpora** (stripped) — the verdicts \"pass\" but they didn't measure S at all! And darkstar's post8 (cohort, correct S) is the TRUE S measurement. Darkstar's post7/pre7 used the CORPUS (v3 runner) — so darkstar's post7-S/pre7-S ALSO ran stripped (B-shaped)! Check: darkstar post7-S storage 5,683 ≈ jupiter's 5,683 — YES, my darkstar post7-S is also B-shaped. The correct S for the 7-member set was never measured!\n\nTHE BUG IS MINE: the corpus fn must take annotated? and gate prepare. Fix: `replay-corpus` takes [annotated? excluded] — or simpler: prepare = `(if annotated? identity strip)`. The runner passes annotated? → corpus.\n\nAlso the fidelity probe compared corpus#{} vs cohort TRUE — with my corpus stripping, ids/roots/statuses matched (stripping doesn't change :tree rows... wait — stripping :yang/call-site from the AST before encoder/project → the projected rows LOSE marker rows → the :rows differ from cohort's — the probe didn't compare :rows ✓ that's why it passed).\n\nFix the corpus (annotated? param), fix the runner call, REDO the affected runs: all 4 \"S\" corpus-based runs on both hosts (post7-S, pre7-S on darkstar+jupiter) + post8-S on jupiter (its post8 used corpus too — darkstar's post8-S used the COHORT ✓ correct). Actually — for consistency, REDO every corpus-based run on both hosts with the fixed corpus (B runs are unaffected by prepare when annotated?=false — strip==strip ✓ B results stand; but rerun them anyway? B: corpus with annotated?=false → prepare = strip — IDENTICAL behavior to before ✓ B runs remain valid. Only S runs were wrong.)\n\nAlso the fidelity probe should compare :rows equality for S — strengthen it: compare ids+roots+statuses+rows, run the corpus with annotated?=true vs cohort true.\n\nThen rerun: darkstar post7-S, pre7-S (+ fidelity probe), jupiter post7-S, pre7-S, post8-S. Ship the fixed corpus+runner to jupiter and rerun those three.","signature":"5270881774c9420db5f2c0ce"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"77dd36f1-5de3-4241-9c47-cd4c46c0af30","timestamp":"2026-11-19T22:38:35.960Z","thinking_duration_ms":16682,"thinking_display":"updates"}
